# Demo/ hashes: t2_route_a.py=95a5408901ec125c  t2_trellis.py=31cd0ee9c68e972b  t2_gmm.py=d064e58c7510c769
# content     : eigenvalue SPECTRUM of sym(Jr), not just its minimum.  ckpt = ckpt/d2sx_N160000_a1.pt
# n           : 48 held-out samples per grid point, 2N = 64 eigenvalues each
# hypothesis  : D2's support is a union of 3L-dim manifolds (L~U{3..8}) in R^64, so the TRUE J
#               has 40..55 eigenvalues AT the PSD boundary; estimation error flips ~half of them.
#               D1's grid-GMM prior has full support, so its true J has no near-zero eigenvalue.

